Issue #12 item G1 -- INV-5(b) mutation evidence
================================================================================

Base commit (parent of this item's own commit): d4941fa2d26f547af79ddcf7dbef4b52989d9a5c

This targets restart-on-panic recovery for the SAME failed unit (INV-5(b)),
not cross-unit isolation -- a panic inside one Tokio task is already caught
at that task's own boundary regardless of supervision, so it can never
propagate to an unrelated sibling task or role; that part (INV-5(a)) is
verified directly, not by this mutation, in
`.agents/issue-12/evidence/G1-evidence.md`'s own "Verify (c)" section and in
this crate's own `tests/g1_integration.rs`.

What was broken and how
------------------------
Two temporary edits, both reverted after capture (confirmed by `git diff`
showing no residue in the final commit):

1. `crates/corvette-media-bridge/src/moq_publish.rs` -- in `run_publish_once`'s
   frame-received arm, a one-line injected panic keyed to a camera literally
   named "cam-target":

       if name == "cam-target" {
           panic!("deliberately injected panic for issue #12 G1's INV-5(b) mutation");
       }

2. A temporary test harness, `crates/corvette-media-bridge/tests/g1_mutation_temp.rs`
   (not committed -- deleted once this log was captured), wiring two real
   cameras through the real `corvette_media_bridge::start` entrypoint against
   a real local `moq-relay`:
   - "cam-target": for the BROKEN run only, its MoQ-publish task was spawned
     via a bare, unsupervised `tokio::spawn` instead of
     `supervise::spawn_supervised_with` (via a temporary
     `Supervised::from_bare` constructor added to `src/supervise.rs` and a
     matching `if camera.name == "cam-target" { ... } else { ... }` branch
     temporarily added to `src/lib.rs::start`'s own per-camera loop, both
     reverted afterward).
   - "cam-healthy": always used the real, correct `spawn_supervised_with`
     pattern, unmodified, as a same-process sibling to verify against.

Both cameras are real `corvette_rtsp_client::client::Client`s dialing
independent `corvette_rtsp_client::mock_camera::MockCamera` instances (issue
#18's own test double, unmodified). Observable signal: whether a brand-new
`moq_net` subscriber can see a camera's broadcast announced by the relay --
`create_broadcast(..., with_announce(true))` announces immediately on
connect, before any frame is read, independent of whether the camera's video
ever resolves a decodable catalog (`MockCamera` never sends real parameter
sets, the same documented limitation `G1-evidence.md` records for the main
integration test).

Command (both runs): `MOQ_RELAY_BIN=<path to the pinned moq-relay binary,
see G1-evidence.md's own R1 build steps> cargo test -p corvette-media-bridge
--test g1_mutation_temp -- --ignored --nocapture --test-threads=1`

