Confirms the defect: `cam-target` never re-announced (its bare-spawned task
died on the panic and nothing restarted it) even after waiting the full
2-second settle window plus a further 10-second fresh-subscribe timeout,
while `cam-healthy` -- sharing the same process, the same relay, the same
mock-camera-driven error-heavy input, differing only in using the real
`spawn_supervised_with` pattern -- stayed reachable throughout. The
`cam-healthy` frame errors visible above ("NAL unit is too short", "SPS NAL
too short") are expected: `MockCamera` fabricates non-decodable payloads (see
`G1-evidence.md`); they demonstrate this crate's own per-frame error handling
tolerates bad input without panicking, which is a separate property from
what this mutation targets.

