Confirms the fix: with the real `spawn_supervised_with` pattern restored,
"cam-target" panics repeatedly (every ~12ms once connected -- the injected
panic fires on the very first frame `MockCamera`'s default 40ms interval
delivers) but its supervisor restarts it every time, redialing and
re-announcing to the relay after each panic, so a fresh subscriber sees it
reachable again well within the timeout. "cam-healthy" never panics and
stays reachable throughout, in both runs -- confirming INV-5(a)'s
cross-unit isolation held unconditionally regardless of which run was
active, exactly as the plan's own text says it must (see G1-evidence.md's
Verify (c) for the direct, non-mutation confirmation of this).

Full revert and re-verification
---------------------------------
After capturing both runs above:
  - `crates/corvette-media-bridge/src/moq_publish.rs`'s injected panic was
    removed.
  - `crates/corvette-media-bridge/src/supervise.rs`'s temporary
    `Supervised::from_bare` was removed.
  - `crates/corvette-media-bridge/src/lib.rs`'s temporary per-camera branch
    was reverted to its original, unconditional `spawn_supervised_with` call.
  - `crates/corvette-media-bridge/tests/g1_mutation_temp.rs` was deleted.

